    "updated_at": "2024-08-02T16:18:01Z",
    "body": "I can speak to `popover`, and it might offer some ideas for the general question?\r\n\r\nThe initial idea was that for forward compat, `<div popover=invalid>` should act as if there was no popover attribute at all, so that if we later add a supported `popover=invalid` value, it hopefully won't break stuff. But we wanted `<div popover>` (empty value) to \"just work\" with the most common behavior of `popover=auto`. Then @emilio raised some good points in https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/533#issuecomment-1219921492 (you can read above that also, for more motivation for different defaults) that triggered a change of the invalid value default to `manual`. But before/after this change, there were different empty-value and missing-value defaults.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
