    "updated_at": "2024-08-14T15:43:32Z",
    "body": "I did mis-speak a bit, in particular about the missing value default. It's unfortunate that it's not called the \"missing attribute default\", since mentally I think of `popover` (without `=something`) as having a missing **value**. However, the logic still stands:\r\n\r\n- `<div popover>` - empty (`\"\"`) value, has the [same behavior](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-popover-none-state) as `auto`.\r\n- `<div popover=invalid>` - *invalid value default* **is `manual`** for the reasons mentioned\r\n- `<div>` - *missing value default* is the **no popover state** for the reasons mentioned.\r\n\r\nSo there are invalid & missing value defaults that are different from each other, which was the original question, I believe.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
